esent, drawn from a different model family wherever one is configured, degrading only to the documented same-family mode — with every selection logged before launch and a non-converging rework loop escalated through the declared approval level, and, where a claimed work item is marked for an in-lane single plan, refuse build output at its making or landing until a pass record binds its plan and Done-when.\""," rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-026 (cross-family second opinions — every prior carrier of this contract demoted as routing machinery, so the sn_refs join forced the mint; SR-155 cites SN-026 too, for the planner pair, but only this row states the second opinion itself), SN-024 (an author cannot judge its own output) and SN-006. One row because routing, scheduling, scoring and escalation are one delivered contract — that the second opinion happens, independently, or its absence is documented — whose mechanics are the component details below it. The row also carries SN-026's DECLARATION and CONSENT half — `docs/agents.toml`'s pair-rows and the `docs/agents-enabled` surface whose presence turns managed selection on. That half had ZERO textual occurrence anywhere in the SR layer while `orphans=0` still held, because an orphan count proves a need has a citing row and never that the row carries the whole need. Managed selection is opt-in by consent rather than by configuration alone: a repository that declares families without dropping the surface has declared a capability, not turned one on, and the row now says so where a check can read it. fan-out re-stamp: the single plan's independent critique is one obligation carried by its briefs and filing and by its gate; the routing children remain separate.\"\"\""," acceptance_criteria = \"A declared review policy of N schedules N independent reviewer sessions; the declared (family x model x tier) pair-rows of the delivered agent registry are the only candidate source, and the declared consent surface's presence is what turns managed selection on — absent, managed selection is off and no row is resolved; present, exactly one row resolves per in-process phase and tier; a configured cross-family draw is preferred and its unavailability degrades to the documented mode, never a silent skip; every selection is logged before launch, never a silent model swap; rework iterates within the declared budget and pages per the declared approval level on exhaustion. The verdict that may clear integration comes from a session minted for that review, or, where reviewer retention is on and the declared final-reviewer setting selects persistence, from a round the coordinator recorded as final for the lane's retained final reviewer, over the whole lane, from its recorded claim to its reviewed tip; iteration rounds between full rounds review only rework since the last reviewed state, answer that round's findings, and never clear integration, whether their session was started fresh or resumed. Where a claimed work item is marked for an in-lane single plan, no build output is accepted at its making or landing until a pass record binds its plan and Done-when; the plan either covers every Done-when item or excludes it with a reason, declares an architectural delta of none, or one carried within its scope. One revision receives a fresh independent critique. If that second critique does not read as an approval, only an accepted dispute dismissal of every blocking or major finding permits the record; otherwise the item goes to the owner. A plan or Done-when changed after the record requires a fresh record. Ticking a Done-when item, or adding evidence to it, does not require a fresh record. Work items whose plan mark is absent, empty, none or dual are not held by this planning requirement; an unrecognized mark is held.\""," priority = \"S\""]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-922\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-922\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-922\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GiajiHJKzEgP8ZRaKb1yhu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
